# Trivy vulnerability suppressions for the filesystem scan
# (.github/workflows/stackpilot-scan.yml, scan-ref: .).
#
# Every entry MUST carry a justification so a future auditor can see exactly
# why the alert was suppressed. Remove an entry the moment its premise changes.

# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 (react-router RSC-mode CSRF bypass): Not applicable.
# This application is a Vite SPA using createBrowserRouter and does not utilize
# React Server Components (RSC); the vulnerable code path requires RSC mode, so
# the attack surface physically does not exist here. The only upstream fix is
# react-router 8.x, a breaking framework major whose regression risk is not
# justified for zero real security gain. Revisit if the app adopts react-router
# RSC mode or migrates to v8.
